## The proposals
  prefetch: l1d_prefetcher=va_ampm_lite, l2_prefetcher=ip_stride, llc_prefetcher=no
    because: Replacing the overly aggressive and inaccurate SPP prefetcher at L2 with a simpler IP stride prefetcher tests whether we can improve L2 hit ratio and reduce bandwidth pollution.
  geometry: l1d_sets=32, l1d_ways=8, l2_sets=1024, l2_ways=8, llc_sets=1024, llc_ways=8
    because: Reducing L1D capacity to 16 KB decreases hit latency from 4 to 3 cycles, testing if the latency reduction benefits the critical path more than the lost capacity harms the miss rate.
  replacement: l2_replacement=ship, llc_replacement=ship
    because: Since L2 suffers from prefetch pollution with zero accuracy and LRU is vulnerable to it, SHiP might better predict reuse distances and mitigate the insertion of useless prefetches.
  concurrency: l2_mshr=32, llc_mshr=64
    because: Reducing L2 MSHRs to 32 tests if constraining the concurrency available to useless prefetches (accuracy 0.00) reduces contention and improves performance, as an earlier sketch showed no benefit to having 64 over 32.

